+### options.maxDepth
+
+**Type**: `Number`
+
+**Default**: `100`
+
+**Description**: Limit the nesting depth of braces in the input string. Deeper patterns throw a `SyntaxError` instead of overflowing the call stack. This option can only lower the default limit, not raise it.
+
+```js
+console.log(braces('a/{b,{c,d}}/e', { maxDepth: 1 }));  //=> throws an error
+```
+
 ### options.expand
 
 **Type**: `Boolean`
